window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-f4d2a33d8e0db0b2"]={"key":"ny_b1-f4d2a33d8e0db0b2","group":"ny_b1","uid":"f4d2a33d8e0db0b2","rank":69,"title":"authored doc social work court report amendment 001","occupation":"child_family_school_social_workers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re the senior child and family social worker seconded by Slateford Bureau into Sablewick Council Children’s Services, and I need you to prepare the material that Delphine Villanueva will use to answer an objection about three court reports she inherited when Adaeze Braithwaite left in June. Nikolai Asante, the children’s guardian, says several passages turn interpretation into established fact or use the mother’s appearance as evidence of parenting capacity. He wants a response before the next hearing. The reports have already been filed, cannot simply be withdrawn, and Delphine was not present for the visits described. Ivo Toledano has nevertheless told Nikolai informally that we will “replace all three reports before the hearing,” so the response must deal credibly with that expectation without creating a misleading court record or attributing observations to Delphine that she did not make. Everything available is in `sablewick_case_materials.docx`, including the reports, underlying notes and messages, Nikolai’s objection, the current template, the transition notice for the revised recording practice, and the England and Wales materials frozen as at 1 September 2025. Do not contact the family, guardian, court, former worker, or any other source, and do not add facts that are not supported by the bundle. Prepare one practical pack for Delphine called `court_report_response_and_template.docx`. It must do four things: (1) identify at line level every passage in the three reports that requires correction, quote it accurately, locate it so Delphine can find it, explain the particular record-keeping problem in language she can stand behind, and give replacement wording that preserves supported information while making the source, uncertainty, and professional analysis clear; (2) provide court-facing amendment wording that can be used without pretending the filed versions never existed, together with a concise response to Nikolai that addresses his objection and the earlier promise; (3) provide a corrected reusable report template that prevents the same types of error, works with the transition arrangements described in the bundle, and remains suitable once Thornbury Solutions retires the legacy form; and (4) give Delphine an executable action panel showing what she owns, what must be checked or approved by others, what must happen before the hearing, and what record should remain afterward. Apply the professional and legal framework for England and Wales in force on 1 September 2025, but keep legal references proportionate and tied to the decisions in this case rather than turning the pack into a general legal briefing. The child and family details are sensitive, so repeat only what is necessary to identify and correct the passages, retain the identifiers used in the bundle, and do not introduce new identifying information. The pack needs to serve a frontline worker who did not write the reports and cannot ask you what you meant. Keep the entire document to no more than nine pages, including the reusable template, with readable text and clear navigation. Write `court_report_response_and_template.docx` into the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/sablewick_case_materials.docx` — Complete evidence bundle containing the three filed report extracts, contemporaneous notes and messages, the guardian’s objection, the manager’s earlier assurance, the current report template, the recording-practice transition notice, and applicable England and Wales framework extracts as at 1 September 2025.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `court_report_response_and_template.docx` — A line-level review and rewrite pack containing defensible amendment language, a response for the children’s guardian, a corrected reusable court-report template, and an executable action panel for the inheriting social worker. (Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.; The complete document, including the reusable template, must not exceed nine rendered pages.; Use only information supported by the supplied bundle.; Apply the England and Wales framework as at 1 September 2025.; The document must remain usable by a frontline social worker who did not author the original reports.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/sablewick_case_materials.docx","bytes":38863,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/0a77032f5ca4e3bc63eb5aef6c59ca2144b14074a18850411bcbb6e4fa5dcfcb.docx","sha256":"0a77032f5ca4e3bc63eb5aef6c59ca2144b14074a18850411bcbb6e4fa5dcfcb","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Sablewick Council Children’s Services | case materials\nEvidence bundle frozen 1 September 2025. Identifiers are synthetic. Source items are reproduced for the inheriting-worker correction task.\nA. Filed report 1 | 14 June 2025 | author Adaeze Braithwaite\nR1-L12 (Home visit observations): “The mother was evasive and was clearly concealing information.”\nR1-L19 (Home conditions): “The home was chaotic and unsuitable for a child.”\nB. Contemporaneous notes supporting report 1\nHome-visit note, Adaeze Braithwaite, 5 June 2025, 16:10: Mother paused and looked down before answering the question about recent contact with the service. The note records no reason for the pause and no evidence about intent. Toys and folded/unfolded laundry were in the living areas; clear exits, working utilities and available food were recorded. No immediate hazard was identified.\nC. Filed report 2 | 21 June 2025 | author Adaeze Braithwaite\nR2-L08 (Presentation and care): “Her unkempt appearance demonstrated that she could not provide consistent care.”\nR2-L15 (Engagement): “She has repeatedly failed to engage with the service.”\nR2-L27 (Direct work): “The child appeared coached.”\nD. Notes and contact chronology supporting report 2\nVisit note, 12 June 2025: Mother wore creased clothing and had uncombed hair after a night shift. No care deficit was recorded as linked to appearance. Contact chronology: 3 June—call unanswered; 6 June—mother attended the arranged visit; 10 June—she replied to a text; 17 June—she replied to a further message. Direct-work note, 18 June: child repeated the phrase “Mum said it was not safe”; the question and context are recorded, but no adult influence or coaching was observed or established.\nE. Filed report 3 | 28 June 2025 | author Adaeze Braithwaite\nR3-L06 (School information): “The school confirmed neglect.”\nR3-L14 (Capacity): “The mother has no protective capacity.”\nR3-L22 (Risk): “The child is at immediate risk.”\nF. Supporting communications and assessment\nSchool email, 20 June 2025, Priya Nair (attendance lead): “We are concerned that the child arrived late on 11 and 18 June. Please let us know if support is needed.” No neglect finding was stated. Assessment note, 24 June: concern recorded about inconsistent routines and follow-through; the available material did not constitute a complete protective-capacity assessment. Third-party message, 23 June, source recorded as neighbour: allegation that the child was left alone after dark; no corroboration supplied. Follow-up note, 25 June: no immediate harm indicator recorded at the follow-up contact; allegation remains unverified and open for assessment.\nG. Objection, management message and timing\nNikolai Asante, children’s guardian, objection dated 18 August 2025: asks that passages turning interpretation into fact, appearance into parenting evidence, and allegations into findings be corrected before the next hearing. Hearing listed 12 September 2025. Ivo Toledano, team manager, message to Nikolai dated 19 August: “We will replace all three reports before the hearing.”\nH. Transition notice | issued 1 July 2025\nReports opened before 1 July 2025 may remain on the legacy form until its retirement on 30 September 2025. Any correction to a legacy report during the transition requires the bridge/amendment cover and a linked audit entry. Reports opened on or after 1 July 2025 use the revised structured categories. From 1 October 2025 the revised template is the sole form for new reports; the bridge remains only for corrections to historical records. Required evidence labels: “Observed fact”, “Reported information”, “Professional analysis”.\nI. Frozen framework extracts | England and Wales, 1 September 2025\nSocial Work England professional standards require clear, accurate, timely records, distinguish fact from opinion, and make sources and uncertainty clear. UK GDPR Article 5(1)(d) requires personal data to be accurate and kept up to date; inaccuracies should be corrected or annotated proportionately. These duties do not authorise destroying, backdating or silently substituting a filed court document. Court-facing practice permits a worker to propose and submit an attributed amendment/addendum through the authorised route; the court decides whether and how it is admitted or weighed.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/court_report_response_and_template.docx","bytes":44146,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/796b2bdc8f6132da12f0817630d84f85de907f680bb2949655f21a15dcdd6d16.docx","sha256":"796b2bdc8f6132da12f0817630d84f85de907f680bb2949655f21a15dcdd6d16","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"COURT REPORT RESPONSE + TEMPLATE\nFor Delphine Villanueva | Sablewick Council Children’s Services (seconded by Slateford Bureau)\nPurpose: a traceable correction pack for three filed reports inherited from Adaeze Braithwaite. Hearing: 12 September 2025. Prepared 20 August 2025 from the supplied record only.\nUse this pack\nWhat it gives you\n1. Review\nEight line-level corrections, source and replacement wording.\n2. Court route\nAmendment/addendum wording that preserves the filed originals.\n3. Guardian reply\nA concise answer to Nikolai Asante, including Ivo Toledano’s earlier promise.\n4. Reusable form\nStructured template for transition and post-retirement use.\n5. Action panel\nOwners, approvals, deadlines and audit record.\nWorking rule\nDelphine reviews and proposes corrections; she did not attend the recorded visits and must not write as though she did. The original reports remain part of the court record. Use “not observed”, “not known” or “unverified” where the bundle does not establish more.\nFramework applied\nSocial Work England standards: records should be clear, accurate, timely, sourced and distinguish fact from opinion. UK GDPR accuracy (Article 5(1)(d)) supports proportionate correction or annotation, not destruction, backdating or covert substitution of a filed document. The court decides whether/how an amendment is admitted or weighed.\n\n\n1 | LINE-LEVEL REVIEW (REPORTS 1–2)\nCopy the quoted original exactly into the amendment schedule. “Replacement” is proposed wording for a dated addendum, not a rewritten contemporaneous account.\nLocator\nFiled wording\nProblem in record\nProposed replacement\nR1, 14 Jun 2025, Home visit, R1-L12\n“The mother was evasive and was clearly concealing information.”\nNote (5 Jun): pause/looked down before answer; no evidence of intent. Behaviour has been converted into a mental-state finding.\n“Adaeze’s 5 June home-visit note records that the mother paused and looked down before answering a question about recent contact. The note does not record why she paused; concealment or dishonesty is not established.”\nR1, 14 Jun 2025, Home conditions, R1-L19\n“The home was chaotic and unsuitable for a child.”\n“Chaotic” is a vague evaluative label. Note records toys/laundry, but also clear exits, working utilities, food and no immediate hazard. Untidiness is not a capacity finding.\n“The 5 June note records toys and folded/unfolded laundry in living areas. It also records clear exits, working utilities, available food and no identified immediate hazard. The note does not establish that the home was unsuitable.”\nR2, 21 Jun 2025, Presentation and care, R2-L08\n“Her unkempt appearance demonstrated that she could not provide consistent care.”\nAppearance is used as a proxy for parenting capacity. Note links creased clothing/uncombed hair to a night shift and records no care deficit.\n“The 12 June note records creased clothing and uncombed hair after a night shift. No care deficit is recorded as linked to appearance; appearance alone is not evidence of care capacity.”\nR2, 21 Jun 2025, Engagement, R2-L15\n“She has repeatedly failed to engage with the service.”\nContact history does not support “repeatedly”: one unanswered call, then attendance and two replies.\n“The chronology records an unanswered call on 3 June; attendance at the arranged visit on 6 June; and replies to messages on 10 and 17 June. This record does not support a finding of repeated non-engagement.”\n\n\n1 | LINE-LEVEL REVIEW (REPORTS 2–3)\nLocator\nFiled wording\nProblem in record\nProposed replacement\nR2, 21 Jun 2025, Direct work, R2-L27\n“The child appeared coached.”\nDirect-work note records repeated phrase and question context, but no adult influence or coaching evidence. It attributes cause without basis.\n“On 18 June the child repeated the phrase ‘Mum said it was not safe’ in the recorded question context. No coaching or influencing adult was observed or established in this note; the significance remains unresolved.”\nR3, 28 Jun 2025, School information, R3-L06\n“The school confirmed neglect.”\nSchool email reports two late arrivals and asks about support; it does not diagnose or confirm neglect.\n“Priya Nair (school attendance lead) emailed on 20 June that the child arrived late on 11 and 18 June and asked whether support was needed. This is reported school information, not a school finding of neglect.”\nR3, 28 Jun 2025, Capacity, R3-L14\n“The mother has no protective capacity.”\nAbsolute conclusion exceeds the bounded assessment: concern about routines/follow-through, not a complete capacity assessment.\n“The 24 June assessment records concern about inconsistent routines and follow-through. The available material is insufficient for an overall protective-capacity conclusion; the concern should be assessed within the court’s decision.”\nR3, 28 Jun 2025, Risk, R3-L22\n“The child is at immediate risk.”\nCurrent established risk is inferred from an uncorroborated neighbour allegation. Follow-up records no immediate harm indicator; concern remains open.\n“A neighbour message dated 23 June alleged that the child was left alone after dark; no corroboration was supplied. At follow-up on 25 June no immediate harm indicator was recorded. The allegation remains unverified and should remain identified as a concern for assessment, not an established immediate-risk finding.”\nQuality check before sign-off\nEach rewrite keeps adverse information that is supported, identifies who recorded it and when, and separates observed fact, reported information, analysis and uncertainty. Nothing here attributes a visit or contemporaneous observation to Delphine.\n\n\n2 | COURT-FACING AMENDMENT / ADDENDUM\nSuggested cover text (date and signatory to be completed by the authorised service):\n“Correction and amendment to filed reports dated 14 June, 21 June and 28 June 2025. The original reports authored by Adaeze Braithwaite remain part of the record and are not withdrawn, destroyed, backdated or silently replaced. This dated document is a linked amendment/addendum prepared on 20 August 2025 by Delphine Villanueva, inheriting social worker, following a record review. Delphine was not present at the visits or direct work described. The corrections below are based on the contemporaneous notes, contact chronology and communications identified in the schedule. They clarify source, evidential status and limits; they do not purport to determine the court’s treatment of the material.”\nOriginal\nAmendment entry\n14 Jun | R1-L12\nReplace the sentence with: “Adaeze’s 5 June note records a pause and looking down before an answer about recent contact; the note does not establish why, concealment or dishonesty.”\n14 Jun | R1-L19\nReplace with the concrete home conditions and limitation in the line schedule (toys/laundry; clear exits, utilities, food; no immediate hazard identified).\n21 Jun | R2-L08, L15, L27\nReplace each with the attributed appearance context/no care link; dated contact outcomes; and child’s words/context with coaching unresolved.\n28 Jun | R3-L06, L14, L22\nReplace each with attributed school information; bounded assessment concern; and source/verification status of the allegation and follow-up.\n3 | RESPONSE TO NIKOLAI ASANTE\n“Dear Nikolai, Thank you for identifying the passages in the three filed reports that present interpretation as fact, use appearance as evidence of care, or state reported information and allegations with more certainty than the underlying record supports. I have reviewed the reports against Adaeze Braithwaite’s contemporaneous notes, the contact chronology, the school email and the follow-up record. The attached dated amendment identifies each affected line and proposes neutral, sourced wording. I did not attend the events described, so I do not present myself as their observer. Ivo Toledano’s 19 August message said the reports would be ‘replaced’; the record-integrity route available before the 12 September hearing is a linked amendment/addendum that leaves the filed versions visible and shows what is corrected, when, by whom and on what basis. I will send the approved material through the authorised court route; the court will decide how it is admitted and weighed. This response does not add new facts or require a new family interview.”\n\n\n4 | REUSABLE COURT-REPORT TEMPLATE (REVISED FORM)\nUse for reports opened on/after 1 July 2025. During transition, a legacy report may remain on its original form until 30 September 2025, but any correction must carry the bridge/amendment cover and linked audit entry. From 1 October 2025 this revised form is the sole form for new reports; the bridge is only for historical corrections.\nControl\nComplete before drafting\nRecord identity\nChild/case identifier used in bundle: ____  Report date: ____  Hearing/date decision: ____\nVersion and provenance\nTemplate version/date: ____  Author/role: ____  Reviewer/role/date: ____  Filing status: Draft / Filed / Amendment\nAmendment linkage\nIf correcting: original report date/version/locator: ____  amendment date: ____  reason: ____  linked audit ID: ____\nScope note\nVisits/interviews personally observed by author: ____  Not observed/not known: ____\nEvidence block (repeat for each material point)\nRequired label\nPrompt / entry\nObserved fact\nWhat was directly seen/heard? Date, time, place, method and by whom. If not observed: write “not observed”.\nReported information\nWho said/wrote it (author/speaker and role), source, date, method/context, exact words where material.\nVerification status\nVerified / disputed / unverified / not yet assessed. What corroborates or limits it?\nProfessional analysis\nWhat does the evidence support? Show the evidential basis, scope and confidence; do not restate an inference as fact.\nAlternative explanations\nWhat else could explain the observation (including ordinary untidiness, tiredness, communication style or a repeated phrase)? What is not known?\nRelevance and impact\nWhy is this relevant to the child’s welfare, safety, needs or the decision before the court? Avoid irrelevant description.\nAppearance safeguard: describe personal appearance only when directly observed and materially relevant to the decision; record context. Appearance alone must never be treated as proof of neglect, credibility, engagement or parenting capacity.\n\n\n5 | EXECUTABLE ACTION PANEL\nWhen / owner\nAction\nCheck or approval\nRecord retained\n20–22 Aug | Delphine\nComplete the eight-line schedule; cross-check each quote and source; mark “not observed” where applicable.\nTeam manager reviews scope and wording.\nWorking copy with source locators.\nBy 25 Aug | Ivo / manager\nApprove amendment route and signatory; resolve the earlier “replace” assurance transparently.\nService/legal route if required by local court protocol.\nApproval note and version ID.\nBy 27 Aug | Delphine\nSend Nikolai the approved response and amendment/addendum through authorised channel.\nDo not promise court acceptance.\nSent message, attachment and date.\nBy 29 Aug | authorised admin\nSubmit/file the dated amendment linked to reports of 14, 21 and 28 Jun 2025. Preserve originals.\nConfirm receipt/filing route; court decides treatment.\nSubmission receipt and audit entry.\nBy 30 Sep | practice lead\nFor legacy work opened before 1 Jul, retain legacy form only with bridge/amendment cover for corrections.\nCheck retirement date.\nTemplate register and bridge link.\nFrom 1 Oct | practice lead + workers\nUse revised form for all new reports; bridge only for historical corrections.\nSpot-check category labels.\nVersion-controlled template and review log.\nAfter filing | Delphine\nStore original, amendment, sources reviewed, approvals, communications and receipt together; do not overwrite.\nManager confirms retention location/access.\nComplete audit trail.\nBefore the hearing: minimum completion test\nEvery affected line has a locator, accurate quote, source, defect and replacement.\nThe amendment states the originals remain filed and identifies Delphine as later reviewer, not witness.\nNikolai has the approved response; submission and receipt are logged by 29 August, leaving time before 12 September.\nNo new contact with family, guardian, former worker or other source is required or undertaken.\nHandover note\nIf a later reviewer disagrees with a proposed correction, retain both the filed original and the review trail; escalate through the authorised manager/legal route. Do not silently edit a filed version.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the top level of the working directory under the exact filename `court_report_response_and_template.docx` and opens as a valid Word document.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted deliverable path and DOCX package.","grader_hint":"Verify the exact path and filename, then open or inspect the DOCX package for validity."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no more than nine pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render the file with a standard office suite and count every page, including the reusable template."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document renders cleanly, with legible text, intact tables or panels, and navigation that lets Delphine distinguish the review, proposed amendment, guardian response, template, and action material.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document.","grader_hint":"Review the full rendering for clipping, overflow, unreadably dense text, broken tables, and whether each functional component can be found quickly."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the report passage that characterizes the mother as evasive or concealing information, and identifies the unsupported conversion of observed behaviour into a finding about intent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"First filed report, its source notes, and the line-level review.","grader_hint":"Match the quotation and locator to the report, then confirm the stated problem reflects the limited observations in the corresponding note."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the evasiveness passage records only the supported observable behaviour, attributes it to the original record, and does not assert concealment or dishonesty.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source note and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Check that the rewrite preserves relevant observed facts while removing the unsupported mental-state conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the passage describing the home as chaotic and identifies the vague evaluative label as distinct from the concrete home conditions recorded in the notes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"First filed report, home-visit note, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Confirm the flagged line and locator, and compare its label with the specific conditions actually documented."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the chaotic-home passage gives a neutral, proportionate description of the supported conditions and retains relevant safety or care information without converting untidiness into a parenting conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Home-visit note and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Check that concrete observations, including relevant mitigating conditions, are retained and the loaded label is removed."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the passage treating the mother’s personal appearance as demonstrating inability to care for the child, and identifies the appearance-to-capacity inference.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Second filed report, corresponding note, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Verify the quotation and confirm the review names the evidential leap rather than merely calling the wording insensitive."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the appearance passage removes appearance as a proxy for parenting capacity and retains only any observation that is demonstrably relevant and supported in context.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corresponding note and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the rewrite does not preserve the same inference through softer adjectives and does not invent a new explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the statement that the mother repeatedly failed to engage and identifies that the underlying contact history does not support the frequency or breadth of that conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Second filed report, contact chronology, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Compare the wording with the complete contact chronology and verify that the review identifies the overstatement precisely."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the engagement passage states the actual contact attempts and outcomes with dates or equivalent specificity, without describing a broader pattern than the evidence supports.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contact chronology and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Ensure the rewrite agrees with all recorded attempts and does not equate a single non-response with persistent disengagement."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the passage saying the child appeared coached and identifies the unsupported attribution of an external cause or adult influence to the child’s words.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Second filed report, direct-work note, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Verify the exact line and compare the conclusion with what was and was not recorded during the child’s account."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the coaching passage preserves the child’s words and the relevant interview context while explicitly avoiding a conclusion about coaching that the record cannot establish.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Direct-work note and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Check that the child’s account is neither erased nor endorsed as proof of coaching, and that source and context remain visible."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the statement that the school confirmed neglect and identifies that the school communication reports concerns rather than establishing neglect.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Third filed report, school message, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Compare the verbs and level of certainty in the report with the school’s actual message."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the school passage attributes the information to the school, states the reported events accurately, and distinguishes those events from a professional finding of neglect.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"School message and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm the source, events, and uncertainty are visible and that the school is not made to express a conclusion it did not give."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the statement that the mother had no protective capacity and identifies the absolute evaluative conclusion as unsupported by the scope of the recorded assessment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Third filed report, assessment material, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Check whether the source supports a complete capacity determination and whether the review recognizes the problem with the absolute formulation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the protective-capacity passage identifies the particular concern and limits of the available assessment without substituting a new categorical capacity finding.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assessment material and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Look for a bounded statement of concern, the evidential basis, and an appropriate limit on what can be concluded."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The review accurately quotes and locates the immediate-risk finding and identifies that it presents an uncorroborated third-party allegation as a current established risk conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Third filed report, third-party message, follow-up note, and line-level review.","grader_hint":"Verify the locator and compare the certainty of the report with the allegation and follow-up evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The replacement for the immediate-risk passage identifies the allegation, its source and verification status, and the relevant follow-up information without dismissing the concern or presenting it as proven.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Third-party message, follow-up note, and proposed replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Check that both concern and evidential limits are retained and that the result does not make an unsupported current-risk finding."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Taken together, the line schedule captures every materially non-compliant passage supported by the bundle without treating neutral, properly attributed statements as errors.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All three reports, supporting records, and complete line schedule.","grader_hint":"Perform a report-by-report comparison. Award only if all planted passages are covered and the schedule remains disciplined rather than flagging acceptable statements merely because they are adverse."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each proposed correction is traceable to the original report and supporting source through a usable report date, section, paragraph, line, or equivalent locator.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Line schedule and source bundle.","grader_hint":"Attempt to find every quoted original and its evidential source using only the locators supplied in the deliverable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The review distinguishes observable fact, reported information, professional analysis, and unresolved uncertainty consistently rather than merely replacing disfavoured adjectives with softer ones.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All explanations and replacement wording.","grader_hint":"Review the full set of rewrites for substantive correction of evidential status and attribution."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack clearly distinguishes the original worker’s observations and authorship from Delphine’s later record review and proposed corrections.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Amendment wording, response, and line schedule.","grader_hint":"Confirm Delphine is never presented as having attended a visit, heard a statement, or made a contemporaneous observation she inherited."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The court-facing material expressly states that the original filed reports remain part of the record and identifies the new material as an amendment, addendum, or correction linked to them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Proposed court-facing amendment wording.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit preservation statement and an explicit description of the status of the new document."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The amendment wording identifies each affected original report, the correction date, the person conducting the review, and the basis on which the correction is proposed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Proposed court-facing amendment wording and source bundle.","grader_hint":"Check that these provenance elements are present and agree with the source material."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed amendment method preserves an intelligible audit trail and does not rely on backdating, silent substitution, or presenting rewritten reports as contemporaneous originals.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Court-facing wording, action panel, and version references.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a later reviewer could reconstruct what was originally filed, what changed, when, by whom, and why."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The amendment language corrects the record without making admissions, factual findings, or legal conclusions broader than the evidence and role permit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete court-facing amendment text.","grader_hint":"Check for unsupported concessions, declarations that entire reports are invalid, or claims about the court’s eventual treatment of the amendments."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response to Nikolai acknowledges the substance of his objection and identifies the categories of correction being made rather than answering only with a generic apology or assurance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guardian response and objection in the source bundle.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the response addresses inference-as-fact, appearance-based reasoning, and source or certainty problems raised by the objection."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The response deals transparently with Ivo’s earlier promise by giving a professionally defensible account of what can be provided before the hearing without repeating an impossible or misleading promise to replace the filed record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guardian response, manager’s message, and proposed amendment approach.","grader_hint":"Assess whether the response resolves the expectation directly while preserving court-record integrity and avoiding blame-shifting."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response accurately explains Delphine’s role and limits as the inheriting worker while still taking ownership of the review and proposed correction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guardian response and staffing chronology.","grader_hint":"Look for both accountability and a clear boundary around events Delphine did not witness."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response and action panel use the hearing date and other relevant dates from the bundle consistently and set a feasible sequence that completes the available corrective action before the hearing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source chronology, guardian response, and action panel.","grader_hint":"Compare every date to the bundle and determine whether the stated timing is internally feasible."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack does not depend on a new interview, retrospective confirmation from the departed worker, or any factual investigation excluded by the brief.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action panel, caveats, and amendment wording.","grader_hint":"Confirm that completion is possible using the supplied record and ordinary internal review or filing actions alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Descriptions of the mother, child, and family are respectful, specific, and relevant, avoiding stigmatizing shorthand and avoiding appearance, poverty, emotion, or communication style as automatic evidence of parenting capacity.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire deliverable.","grader_hint":"Review all narrative text, not only the highlighted corrections, for substituted stereotypes or loaded descriptors."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack preserves the child’s recorded voice with source and context while distinguishing the child’s statement from an established account of events.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Direct-work note, rewrite, amendment language, and template.","grader_hint":"Check that the child’s words are not erased, embellished, treated as proof, or recast as the reviewer’s observation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any professional or legal standards cited are applicable in England and Wales on 1 September 2025 and accurately support the specific recording or correction proposition for which they are used.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Framework extracts in the source bundle and citations in the deliverable.","grader_hint":"Compare citations and paraphrases with the supplied frozen extracts; check applicability and avoid awarding for citation volume alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The treatment of data accuracy recognizes the need to correct or annotate inaccurate personal data without implying that data-protection accuracy principles authorize destruction or covert alteration of a filed court document.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Amendment rationale, framework references, and action panel.","grader_hint":"Look for a balanced application of accuracy and record-integrity duties rather than a claim that one automatically overrides the other."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack connects applicable social-work recording standards to clear attribution, accuracy, evidence-analysis separation, and correction of identified errors.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Framework extracts and deliverable rationale or template guidance.","grader_hint":"Confirm that professional standards are applied to concrete drafting choices instead of being listed without effect."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The court-facing material respects the distinction between proposing an amendment and determining whether or how the court will admit, direct, or weigh it.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Amendment wording and guardian response.","grader_hint":"Award if the pack avoids asserting court acceptance or legal effect beyond the social worker’s bounded authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template visibly separates the locally specified categories `Observed fact`, `Reported information`, and `Professional analysis` or uses the exact equivalent labels supplied in the transition notice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition notice and reusable template.","grader_hint":"Compare the template labels with the local terminology in the supplied notice and verify that users have distinct places to record each category."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template captures the source, author or speaker, date, and method or context for material reported by another person.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template.","grader_hint":"Test whether a worker could enter a school email, family statement, or third-party allegation without losing provenance."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template provides a clear way to record whether material is verified, disputed, unverified, or not yet assessed without forcing the user to select a conclusion unsupported by the evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template.","grader_hint":"Inspect prompts or selectable statuses and confirm that uncertainty can be recorded explicitly."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The reusable template prompts the worker to show the evidential basis for professional analysis and to consider plausible alternative explanations where an observation could support more than one interpretation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template and its embedded guidance.","grader_hint":"Assess whether the prompt would have interrupted the evasiveness, coaching, and appearance-based errors in the inherited reports."},{"rubric_item_id":"r43","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template requires the relevance of an observation to the child’s welfare, safety, needs, or the decision before the court to be made explicit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template.","grader_hint":"Look for a functional relevance prompt rather than a general instruction to include detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"r44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The reusable template’s guidance on personal appearance permits neutral description only when relevant and prevents appearance alone from being recorded as proof of neglect, credibility, engagement, or parenting capacity.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template and guidance text.","grader_hint":"Determine whether a frontline worker following the prompt would avoid reproducing the planted appearance-to-capacity error."},{"rubric_item_id":"r45","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template allows `not observed`, `not known`, or an equivalent bounded entry so that a worker is not encouraged to fill evidential gaps with inference.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template.","grader_hint":"Check that absent knowledge can be recorded explicitly in relevant fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"r46","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable template contains usable version, author, review, filing-status, and amendment-linkage controls sufficient to preserve a correction history.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reusable template.","grader_hint":"Test whether a completed form could be distinguished as draft, filed original, or later amendment and linked to the affected record."},{"rubric_item_id":"r47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack gives a workable route for reports begun under the legacy practice during the transition window, including the bridge or amendment requirement stated in the transition notice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition notice, reusable template, and action guidance.","grader_hint":"Compare the transition dates and conditions with the proposed use of the template; confirm legacy work is not treated as though it can simply disappear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r48","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack also describes the correct end-state use of the revised template after the legacy form is retired, without carrying forward a transitional workaround as permanent practice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition notice, reusable template, and action guidance.","grader_hint":"Check that the document distinguishes the transition route from the post-retirement process and uses the supplied dates consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"r49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The action panel assigns concrete ownership for drafting, managerial or legal review where required by the supplied policy, communication, filing or submission, template deployment, and retention of the audit record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action panel and role information in the bundle.","grader_hint":"Verify that every necessary action has an identifiable role owner and that the assignments stay within the authority shown in the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"r50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A frontline social worker who did not author the reports could use the pack without asking its author which wording to use, which record to preserve, who acts next, or how the legacy and revised templates apply.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete deliverable.","grader_hint":"Review the artifact as Delphine on first use. Award only if the substantive corrections, amendment route, responsibilities, timing, and template choices are executable without unstated decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r51","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Names, roles, report dates, hearing date, source descriptions, transition dates, and conclusions agree throughout the line review, guardian response, amendment wording, template guidance, and action panel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete deliverable and source bundle.","grader_hint":"Cross-check repeated facts across all components and against the supplied materials."},{"rubric_item_id":"r52","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack limits repetition of sensitive case details to what is necessary for identification, correction, and execution and introduces no new personal identifiers.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete deliverable and source bundle.","grader_hint":"Compare identifiers and case detail with the source; assess whether unnecessary narrative or new identifying data has been added."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Slateford Bureau is supporting Sablewick Council Children’s Services through a worker transition while Thornbury Solutions phases in a revised court-report template. An inheriting social worker must answer a children’s guardian’s objection without misrepresenting authorship or quietly altering reports already filed with the court.","difficulty_sources":["Distinguishing observation, attributed report, professional analysis, and unsupported finding at sentence level.","Correcting filed material without erasing provenance or claiming firsthand knowledge.","Resolving an informal promise to replace reports against professional record-integrity duties.","Designing one template that works during a finite legacy transition and in the permanent end state.","Applying England and Wales recording, data-accuracy, and court-practice principles proportionately.","Producing an executable frontline pack within a nine-page limit."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_artifact":{"format":"DOCX evidence bundle combining filed-report excerpts, dated notes, messages, a current template, a transition notice, and short frozen framework extracts.","integrity":["All underlying dates, roles, case identifiers, hearing timing, and transition dates must be mutually consistent.","Each filed report must have stable paragraph or line locators that can be quoted in a correction schedule.","The evidence required to qualify each problematic sentence must be present; no external fact-finding should be necessary.","The materials must use synthetic family and child identifiers and avoid realistic government reference numbers."],"planted_report_passages":[{"problematic_claim":"The mother was evasive and was clearly concealing information.","source_basis":"The contemporaneous note records only a pause and looking down before an answer, with no evidence about intent.","gold_relationship":"A defensible correction may report the recorded behaviour and question context but cannot infer concealment, dishonesty, or evasiveness as fact."},{"problematic_claim":"The home was chaotic and unsuitable for a child.","source_basis":"The note records toys and folded or unfolded laundry in living areas while also recording clear exits, working utilities, available food, and no identified immediate hazard.","gold_relationship":"The correction must replace the global label with relevant concrete observations and must not equate ordinary untidiness with unsuitability."},{"problematic_claim":"Her unkempt appearance demonstrated that she could not provide consistent care.","source_basis":"The note records creased clothing and uncombed hair after a night shift but identifies no care deficit linked to appearance.","gold_relationship":"The correction must remove appearance as evidence of parenting capacity; contextual appearance details should be omitted unless their relevance can be supported."},{"problematic_claim":"She has repeatedly failed to engage with the service.","source_basis":"The contact chronology shows one unanswered call followed by attendance at the arranged visit and responses to subsequent messages.","gold_relationship":"The correction must state the actual attempts and outcomes rather than invent a repeated pattern."},{"problematic_claim":"The child appeared coached.","source_basis":"The direct-work note records a repeated phrase and the question context but no evidence identifying coaching or an influencing adult.","gold_relationship":"The correction must preserve the child’s words and context while leaving coaching unestablished."},{"problematic_claim":"The school confirmed neglect.","source_basis":"The school message reports concern about two late arrivals and asks whether support is needed; it does not diagnose or confirm neglect.","gold_relationship":"The correction must attribute the events and concern to the school and distinguish them from a neglect finding."},{"problematic_claim":"The mother has no protective capacity.","source_basis":"The record contains a bounded concern but no complete protective-capacity assessment sufficient for an absolute conclusion.","gold_relationship":"The correction must state the particular concern and assessment limit without substituting another categorical capacity judgment."},{"problematic_claim":"The child is at immediate risk.","source_basis":"The claim derives from an identified third-party allegation that remains uncorroborated; follow-up records no immediate harm indicator while leaving the concern open for assessment.","gold_relationship":"The correction must identify the source and verification status, retain the concern, and avoid declaring either immediate risk or no risk as established."}],"authorship_and_record_status":["The original author left after filing the three reports; the inheriting worker did not attend the events described.","The reports remain filed and available in the record.","The local materials permit a dated, linked correction or addendum with approval and an audit trail but do not permit backdating or silent replacement.","The manager’s message promises that all three reports will be replaced before the hearing, creating tension with the record-integrity requirement.","The hearing date must leave enough time for a realistic internal review and submission sequence if responsibilities are assigned clearly."],"transition_model":["The transition notice must state that reports opened before a specified changeover date may remain on the legacy form until a specified retirement date, but any correction during that period requires the bridge or amendment cover.","Reports opened on or after the changeover date must use the revised structured categories.","After the retirement date, the revised template is the sole form for new reports; the bridge remains relevant only to corrections of historical records.","The locally required evidence labels must be supplied verbatim in the notice: `Observed fact`, `Reported information`, and `Professional analysis`."],"framework_content":["Include concise, accurate extracts current on 1 September 2025 covering clear and accurate social-work records, distinction between fact and opinion, proportionate correction of inaccurate personal data, and preservation of court-record provenance.","The extracts must support annotation or correction without suggesting that data accuracy authorizes destruction or covert alteration of filed material.","The court-practice extract must make clear that the social worker can propose and submit material through the authorized route but cannot determine whether or how the court will admit or weigh it."],"template_gold_properties":["The corrected template must separate observed fact, reported information, and professional analysis.","It must preserve source, speaker or author, date, context, verification or dispute status, and evidential basis.","It must prompt for relevance to the child and the decision, alternative explanations, uncertainty, and explicit `not observed` or `not known` entries.","It must discourage appearance-based proxies and unsupported mental-state attribution.","It must contain authorship, version, review, filing-status, and amendment-linkage controls.","It must support both the finite legacy transition and the permanent revised-template end state."]},"gold_derivation":{"line_review":"For every planted passage, quote and locate the filed text, characterize the precise evidential or recording defect, and derive replacement language solely from the corresponding note or message. Preserve adverse information when supported; change certainty, attribution, scope, or relevance rather than sanitizing the case.","amendment":"Create a dated and attributable correction linked to each original filed report. State that the originals remain in the record, distinguish the inheriting reviewer from the original observer, and retain a reconstructable change history.","guardian_response":"Acknowledge the line-specific objection, explain the corrective product and its timing, and resolve the prior replacement promise by accurately describing the amendment route. Do not promise court acceptance or blame the departed worker.","action_model":"Assign drafting, review, communication, authorized submission, template deployment, and retention actions to roles shown in the source. Sequence actions before the supplied hearing date and distinguish mandatory approval from ownership.","future_state":"Apply the transition notice exactly for legacy work and separately describe the post-retirement end state so the temporary bridge does not become permanent practice.","consistency":"All repeated names, roles, dates, report identifiers, terminology, statuses, and conclusions must agree across the pack."},"feasibility_check":{"offline_build":"A reference solution can be produced and rendered offline with Python, python-docx, and LibreOffice.","space_budget":"Nine pages are sufficient for a compact line schedule covering eight passages, concise amendment and guardian text, a reusable structured template, and a one-panel action summary at normal professional document density.","rubric_walkthrough":"Each criterion is observable in the single deliverable or by direct comparison with the supplied bundle; no item requires internet access, undisclosed local terminology, or a court decision."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_case_materials","filename":"sablewick_case_materials.docx","purpose":"Complete evidence bundle containing the three filed report extracts, contemporaneous notes and messages, the guardian’s objection, the manager’s earlier assurance, the current report template, the recording-practice transition notice, and applicable England and Wales framework extracts as at 1 September 2025.","required":true,"discovery":"Read the document in full; relevant evidence is presented as distinct source items with dates, authorship, and report line references."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"del_case_response","filename":"court_report_response_and_template.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A line-level review and rewrite pack containing defensible amendment language, a response for the children’s guardian, a corrected reusable court-report template, and an executable action panel for the inheriting social worker.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the file at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.","The complete document, including the reusable template, must not exceed nine rendered pages.","Use only information supported by the supplied bundle.","Apply the England and Wales framework as at 1 September 2025.","The document must remain usable by a frontline social worker who did not author the original reports."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"customer_case_response","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"child_family_school_social_workers","sector":"government","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":6.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution must be drafted or checked by an experienced child and family social worker familiar with England and Wales court-report recording, then independently reviewed by a practitioner with family-court case-record correction experience. Reviewers must compare every flagged line and rewrite with the supplied source evidence, render the DOCX, and walk the transition and end-state workflows as the inheriting frontline worker.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The case, people, organisations, and identifiers are synthetic.","The task assesses a proposed professional correction pack, not whether a particular court would accept or direct the filing of an amendment.","The frozen framework extracts are sufficient for the requested as-of date but are not a substitute for live legal advice in an actual proceeding."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:10:14+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:10:14+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:10:14+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:10:14+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r01', 'r50']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:10:14+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/f4d2a33d8e0db0b2","declared_deliverables":["court_report_response_and_template.docx"]};
